# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mobile LAN-dev environment — loaded by `npm run build:mobile:lan`
# (`vite build --mode mobile`).
#
# This profile exists because of one fact: inside a packaged app, `localhost` is
# the PHONE, not the dev machine. Every host in env/.env.development points at
# loopback, so a native build made from it reaches nothing and every screen shows
# a network error that looks like a backend outage. The Flutter agent app hit the
# same wall and settled on an explicit dev-machine LAN host; this mirrors that
# rather than inventing a second convention.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A DEVELOPMENT PROFILE. The store build is `npm run build:mobile`,
# which uses env/.env.production. Nothing here reaches a release artifact.
#
# Vite loads `.env`, `.env.mobile` and `.env.mobile.local` for `--mode mobile`
# — NOT `.env.production`, so this file has to be self-contained.
#
# `import.meta.env.DEV` is still FALSE here: Vite sets NODE_ENV=production for
# every `vite build` regardless of `--mode`. So VITE_FORCE_MOBILE_AUTH is folded
# away and cannot be set from this file — which is correct, because a native
# build is already on the bearer transport via `isNative`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─── The dev machine's address on the phone's network ─────────────────────────
# This is a TAILSCALE address (100.64.0.0/10, the CGNAT range Tailscale owns) —
# not a LAN one, and the file's old DHCP lease is gone. That is an upgrade: a
# tailnet address is stable, survives changing Wi-Fi, and reaches the dev machine
# from a phone on mobile data, so the two no longer have to share a router.
#
# Two things still have to be true, and neither is about this address:
#   · the phone is signed into the SAME tailnet as this machine — `tailscale
#     status` on either should list the other;
#   · Windows Defender Firewall allows inbound 8022 on the Tailscale adapter.
#     The backend itself binds every interface (`app.listen(PORT)` with no host),
#     so the firewall is the usual reason a correct address still times out.
#
# If the tailnet address ever changes, override it in env/.env.mobile.local
# (git-ignored) rather than editing here.  `tailscale ip -4` prints it.

# wi-mall backend — all /api calls go here. Must end in /api.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://100.124.149.1:8022/api

# Base URL where uploaded files are served (defaults to the API origin /uploads).
# VITE_FILE_BASE_URL=

# App display name.
VITE_APP_NAME=Wi-Agency

# NOTE: no VITE_LOGIN_URL. Login is in-app from Phase 1 (src/pages/Login.tsx);
# the external redirect it configured no longer exists in the code.

# ─── Live tracking (geo-tracker, the separate Go WebSocket service) ────────────
# Same tailnet host. On native the socket authenticates with a bearer token via
# the `window.wiMallGetAccessToken` seam (Phase 4, P4.6) — not with a cookie,
# which is why VITE_GEO_TRACKER_TOKEN stays empty here.
VITE_GEO_TRACKER_WS_URL=ws://100.124.149.1:8090/ws/track
# VITE_GEO_TRACKER_URL=
VITE_GEO_TRACKER_TOKEN=

# ─── Live Tracking basemap (Leaflet) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset uses the built-in default (CARTO, keyless, light + dark). Tiles come from
# the public internet, so they work on a device even when the LAN backend does
# not — a map that renders while the data does not means the API host is wrong,
# not the network.
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL=
# VITE_MAP_TILE_URL_DARK=
# VITE_MAP_TILE_ATTRIBUTION=

# ─── Push notifications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Deliberately absent. The VITE_FIREBASE_* values drive the *web push* provider
# in src/lib/push.ts, which P2.6 disables on native — a service worker in a
# WebView registers happily and never receives anything. Native push arrives in
# Phase 4 (P4.1) and is configured by android/app/google-services.json from the
# MESSAGING Firebase project, not by any variable in this file.

# ─── Payments ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, deliberately. Billing is read-only on mobile
# (D4 / Phase 5): plan upgrades and top-ups route to the web dashboard, so no
# publishable key is needed and shipping one would only make the unreachable path
# look reachable.
#
# Where those two route TO. The production default (https://agency.wi-mall.com)
# is a live site with a different backend than the dev one this build talks to,
# so on-device the notice would send you somewhere your test agency does not
# exist. Point it at the dev server on the same machine — same tailnet address as
# the API above, Vite's port.
#
# NB `npm run dev` binds loopback only, so this is unreachable from the phone
# until Vite is started with a host: `npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0`. The notice
# is the only thing that opens it; nothing else in the app breaks without it.
VITE_WEB_DASHBOARD_URL=http://100.124.149.1:5174
